## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to apply public announcements to epistemic models and design a practical solver that scales with model size.

## Key Concepts
- Kripke models and accessibility relations
- Public announcements and product update
- Knowledge operator Ki and post-update evaluation
- Linear-time propagation and fixpoint reasoning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal representation and product update sketch
function productUpdate(W, relations, V, pSet) {
  const Wp = W.filter(w => pSet.has(w));
  const Rp = {};
  for (const [AG, rel] of Object.entries(relations)) {
    Rp[AG] = new Map();
    for (const w of Wp) {
      Rp[AG].set(w, rel.get(w).filter(v => pSet.has(v)));
    }
  }
  return { W: Wp, relations: Rp };
}

function knows(pSet, w, agentRel) {
  const targets = agentRel.get(w) || [];
  return targets.every(u => pSet.has(u));
}
``` 

